# Pairs with ReaderNeverPassesHole. The consumer is clamped at the allocator's
# head rather than at the durable-contiguous watermark (WalShippingWatermark),
# so with flushes completing out of order it reads past a still-unfilled hole.
MODULE: ReaderNeverPassesHoleConsumerIgnoresWatermark
TARGET: ReaderNeverPassesHole
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the consumer is shown offsets above an in-flight append
PERTURBS: Consume

--- FIND
    /\ ConsumeFrom < Watermark
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the horizon ignores in-flight flushes.
    /\ ConsumeFrom < next
--- END